(6218286, 917080, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Wendy. Fantastic shot.</td>', 'Congratulations, Wendy. Fantastic shot.', '2010-11-10 01:03:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218412, 916636, 20799, '<td valign="top">The wildlife is outside, LOL! I love this! Don''t you love when the audience totally misses the point? Had one in Innocent Bystander getting similar reactions. Wasn''t this good, though. Being a follower of your work, must agree with Bear_Music that this is not one of your typical takes. Still, it''s an amazing photo!</td>', 'The wildlife is outside, LOL! I love this! Don''t you love when the audience totally misses the point? Had one in Innocent Bystander getting similar reactions. Wasn''t this good, though. Being a follower of your work, must agree with Bear_Music that this is not one of your typical takes. Still, it''s an amazing photo!', '2010-11-10 04:12:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218520, 917080, 106109, '<td valign="top">What a killer shot!! I guess I can forget about the VA Wildlife contest, eh? This is fantastic. A big congrats.  --Rick</td>', 'What a killer shot!! I guess I can forget about the VA Wildlife contest, eh? This is fantastic. A big congrats.  --Rick', '2010-11-10 07:23:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218644, 917080, 51269, '<td valign="top">HUGE Congrats , Wendy- spectacular shot !!!!</td>', 'HUGE Congrats , Wendy- spectacular shot !!!!', '2010-11-10 09:22:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218649, 917071, 51269, '<td valign="top">Magnificent ! Congratulations !</td>', 'Magnificent ! Congratulations !', '2010-11-10 09:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218684, 917080, 51597, '<td valign="top">Fabulous!!  Huge Congrats..</td>', 'Fabulous!!  Huge Congrats..', '2010-11-10 09:47:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6219619, 917071, 113591, '<td valign="top">What I want to know is how did you get the stags to battle right under the studio lights? Hehe. Lighting is soooo perfect. I have come back to this photo numerous times, can''t get enough of it.</td>', 'What I want to know is how did you get the stags to battle right under the studio lights? Hehe. Lighting is soooo perfect. I have come back to this photo numerous times, can''t get enough of it.', '2010-11-11 00:46:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6219680, 917505, 54799, '<td valign="top">mindblowing</td>', 'mindblowing', '2010-11-11 05:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6220775, 917505, 42198, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i>Haha! right! I should try my best to make everything symmetrical and submit to websites other than dpc. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Actually I noticed the feathers on his chest aren''t symmetrical either.<br/> <br/>:-p</td>', 'Originally posted by william88:Haha! right! I should try my best to make everything symmetrical and submit to websites other than dpc.  Actually I noticed the feathers on his chest aren''t symmetrical either. :-p', '2010-11-12 09:37:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6220871, 916313, 53814, '<td valign="top">excellent</td>', 'excellent', '2010-11-12 12:10:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6220941, 917080, 11078, '<td valign="top">I love it so well done Congratulations</td>', 'I love it so well done Congratulations', '2010-11-12 13:39:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221055, 917451, 54446, '<td valign="top">Great wildlife image, if the challenge included insects.</td>', 'Great wildlife image, if the challenge included insects.', '2010-11-12 17:01:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221104, 916406, 61315, '<td valign="top">Congrats on top 10 for your cute little turtle! It looks like he''s smiling - nice pose. :-)</td>', 'Congrats on top 10 for your cute little turtle! It looks like he''s smiling - nice pose. :-)', '2010-11-12 18:25:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221328, 917080, 18450, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous shot! Congratulations!!!</td>', 'Gorgeous shot! Congratulations!!!', '2010-11-13 03:35:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221615, 916460, 51269, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture !</td>', 'Excellent capture !', '2010-11-13 12:25:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221767, 917505, 38032, '<td valign="top">This is insane. Just impossible.  Congrats.</td>', 'This is insane. Just impossible.  Congrats.', '2010-11-13 18:56:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6221768, 917051, 38032, '<td valign="top">fantastic frozen moment.</td>', 'fantastic frozen moment.', '2010-11-13 18:58:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222195, 917505, 112828, '<td valign="top">What a shame!  So sorry about your DQ... So what image area did you extend anyway???</td>', 'What a shame!  So sorry about your DQ... So what image area did you extend anyway???', '2010-11-14 13:59:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222204, 917461, 97166, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t know what''s funnier, you shoehorning another zoo shot in a wildlife challenge or Simms "shooting fish in a barrel" calling you out on it.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Much ado about nothing. If you ask someone if a lynx is an example of wildlife they''ll say ABSOLUTELY, but a stray siamese cat would get hammered by voters even if it had never seen a house in its life. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Meh. Like getting "called out" by someone taking a photo of deer in a nature preserve is any different anyway, on the grand scale.</td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: Originally posted by yanko: I don''t know what''s funnier, you shoehorning another zoo shot in a wildlife challenge or Simms "shooting fish in a barrel" calling you out on it. Much ado about nothing. If you ask someone if a lynx is an example of wildlife they''ll say ABSOLUTELY, but a stray siamese cat would get hammered by voters even if it had never seen a house in its life.   Meh. Like getting "called out" by someone taking a photo of deer in a nature preserve is any different anyway, on the grand scale.', '2010-11-14 14:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222232, 917080, 68504, '<td valign="top">Really fine. I also enjoyed the full set on flicker some of which seemed at least as good as your blue ribboner.</td>', 'Really fine. I also enjoyed the full set on flicker some of which seemed at least as good as your blue ribboner.', '2010-11-14 15:14:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222233, 917015, 68504, '<td valign="top">Aha.  The smoothness of the 5d?  No credit to the gull choreographer? Nice yellow, very nice.</td>', 'Aha.  The smoothness of the 5d?  No credit to the gull choreographer? Nice yellow, very nice.', '2010-11-14 15:18:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222237, 916636, 68504, '<td valign="top">Even better 2nd and 3rd looking. The force of light!</td>', 'Even better 2nd and 3rd looking. The force of light!', '2010-11-14 15:27:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222255, 916579, 3746, '<td valign="top">YES!! Finally in the top ten where it deserved to be!</td>', 'YES!! Finally in the top ten where it deserved to be!', '2010-11-14 15:49:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222260, 917015, 30364, '<td valign="top">So ... I had indeed underestimated your gulls at 4th pick.  Sorry bout that!  This might be the first time ever that one of my top picks got a <i>rea</i>l ribbon as opposed to the contrarian type.  Congrats, Robert.</td>', 'So ... I had indeed underestimated your gulls at 4th pick.  Sorry bout that!  This might be the first time ever that one of my top picks got a real ribbon as opposed to the contrarian type.  Congrats, Robert.', '2010-11-14 16:03:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222268, 917015, 102278, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful ballet. Great shot Robert.</td>', 'This is a beautiful ballet. Great shot Robert.', '2010-11-14 16:10:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222431, 916636, 119419, '<td valign="top">..Were you the earth, dear Love, and I the skies,	 <br/>  My love should shine on you like to the Sun, <br/>  And look upon you with ten thousand eyes...</td>', '..Were you the earth, dear Love, and I the skies,	   My love should shine on you like to the Sun,   And look upon you with ten thousand eyes...', '2010-11-14 19:17:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222459, 917015, 28882, '<td valign="top">i''ll bet you could be making some money with this one.  nice.</td>', 'i''ll bet you could be making some money with this one.  nice.', '2010-11-14 19:50:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6222640, 917015, 28742, '<td valign="top">Wow - a lucky break! Congrats Robert!</td>', 'Wow - a lucky break! Congrats Robert!', '2010-11-14 23:45:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6223348, 916532, 17507, '<td valign="top">I enjoy the extreme grain here - it gives this photo a sense of rawness it wouldn''t have otherwise, and breathes life into the openness of the sky.</td>', 'I enjoy the extreme grain here - it gives this photo a sense of rawness it wouldn''t have otherwise, and breathes life into the openness of the sky.', '2010-11-15 10:20:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6223432, 917015, 67237, '<td valign="top">what a fantastic capture!!!<br/>huge congrats on the ribbon<br/>that makes 2 yellows in a row!</td>', 'what a fantastic capture!!!huge congrats on the ribbonthat makes 2 yellows in a row!', '2010-11-15 11:39:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6223745, 917505, 101702, '<td valign="top">After seeing your original file, you did a really sweet job in photoshop. Pity it was outside the rules, and got DQ''d. Does not take away from the fact that it''s a great photo and was expertly "improved".</td>', 'After seeing your original file, you did a really sweet job in photoshop. Pity it was outside the rules, and got DQ''d. Does not take away from the fact that it''s a great photo and was expertly "improved".', '2010-11-15 17:19:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6224076, 917024, 24454, '<td valign="top">I LOVE this!  I love the perspective.</td>', 'I LOVE this!  I love the perspective.', '2010-11-15 23:43:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6224527, 917071, 122896, '<td valign="top">Hey Alex, is it my imagination or you actually came up to second place from the third? It is very well deserved, by the way, just being a bit puzzled, that''s all. I love this photo.</td>', 'Hey Alex, is it my imagination or you actually came up to second place from the third? It is very well deserved, by the way, just being a bit puzzled, that''s all. I love this photo.', '2010-11-16 15:19:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6224529, 917505, 36606, '<td valign="top">wtf! no way. I would say the rules must be changed. Amazing shot nevertheless.</td>', 'wtf! no way. I would say the rules must be changed. Amazing shot nevertheless.', '2010-11-16 15:27:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6224572, 917505, 68586, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by coryboehne:</b></div><hr/><i> What a shame!  So sorry about your DQ... So what image area did you extend anyway??? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The area to the left of his left wing - originally the wing appeared to just get clipped by the edge of the frame - afterwards the shot was symmetrical.<br/> <br/>Hard to argue that the shot wasn''t clearly altered (and so against the rules) - but I agree that the remedial work was first class - as is the image itself.</td>', 'Originally posted by coryboehne: What a shame!  So sorry about your DQ... So what image area did you extend anyway???   The area to the left of his left wing - originally the wing appeared to just get clipped by the edge of the frame - afterwards the shot was symmetrical. Hard to argue that the shot wasn''t clearly altered (and so against the rules) - but I agree that the remedial work was first class - as is the image itself.', '2010-11-16 16:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6224837, 917505, 59267, '<td valign="top">I have deleted about 80 percent of all my hummingbird shots after each shooting session. There are 2296 hummingbird photos remain in my hard drive. That mean in about 11480 shots, there is only one shot look exactly straight into lens. To me, it''s very rare chance. I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot. That''s why I had tried my best to repair the minor imperfection. As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare. I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.<br/>My another shot here <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=883558" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1213/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883558.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1213/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883558.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1213/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883558.jpg"/></a> was also a rare chance because it is usually very hard to focus when there are leaves or flowers behind humer and its beak is not aligned to a flower.<br/>Now both of my ribboned hummingbirds end up like this due to the conflicting rules. What should I say? It''s not worth doing any effort for dpc.<br/>As I mentioned before in this killer shot <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=914918" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1283/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_914918.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1283/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_914918.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1283/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_914918.jpg"/></a> (DQed by the same rule). The consequence of too many rules and cruel DQ plus a broken voting system is making the site less attractive than other photography communities. But what can we do? all I can do is let it sink, let it sink, let it sink. Oh, sorry about the typo. It''s the season of let it snow, let it snow, let it snow.<br/> <br/>You can do almost unlimited things on a real large community site like this one.<br/><a href="//artistwebsites.com/?affiliateid=A45806" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//fineartamerica.com/BannerArtistWebsitesBlack468x60.jpg'', strrpos(''//fineartamerica.com/BannerArtistWebsitesBlack468x60.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//fineartamerica.com/BannerArtistWebsitesBlack468x60.jpg"/></a> <br/>A paid member has a dedicated customizable homepage and can even host a group and contests. How dpc can do to beat them?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-11-16 20:42:08.</i></td>', 'I have deleted about 80 percent of all my hummingbird shots after each shooting session. There are 2296 hummingbird photos remain in my hard drive. That mean in about 11480 shots, there is only one shot look exactly straight into lens. To me, it''s very rare chance. I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot. That''s why I had tried my best to repair the minor imperfection. As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare. I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.My another shot here  was also a rare chance because it is usually very hard to focus when there are leaves or flowers behind humer and its beak is not aligned to a flower.Now both of my ribboned hummingbirds end up like this due to the conflicting rules. What should I say? It''s not worth doing any effort for dpc.As I mentioned before in this killer shot  (DQed by the same rule). The consequence of too many rules and cruel DQ plus a broken voting system is making the site less attractive than other photography communities. But what can we do? all I can do is let it sink, let it sink, let it sink. Oh, sorry about the typo. It''s the season of let it snow, let it snow, let it snow. You can do almost unlimited things on a real large community site like this one. A paid member has a dedicated customizable homepage and can even host a group and contests. How dpc can do to beat them?', '2010-11-16 20:09:25.000000', '2010-11-16 20:42:08.000000', 0),
(6225864, 916406, 100831, '<td valign="top">He is most definitely enjoying the moment. And you brought out the best in him! I love this one.</td>', 'He is most definitely enjoying the moment. And you brought out the best in him! I love this one.', '2010-11-17 12:30:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6228840, 917505, 34938, '<td valign="top">I reckon there''s a big difference between mine and yours in that you added a wingtip. I simply did a selective desaturation which I thought was in the rules. Mine was simply a black and white layer over a colour layer and a mask to reveal the colour. I am sorry about your dq William, they are not nice. :(</td>', 'I reckon there''s a big difference between mine and yours in that you added a wingtip. I simply did a selective desaturation which I thought was in the rules. Mine was simply a black and white layer over a colour layer and a mask to reveal the colour. I am sorry about your dq William, they are not nice. :(', '2010-11-21 02:51:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6228841, 917505, 34938, '<td valign="top">Great job on the edit though... :)</td>', 'Great job on the edit though... :)', '2010-11-21 02:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6229940, 917505, 63503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> .................... I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You didn''t have to give it up at all! you could have just placed it in your portfolio, or entered it in 1x (for free) or the site you gave a link to<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> .................... As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The rule actually states: "clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections within any capture used.", it is a bit hard to interpret that as allowing for <u><i>cloning in</i></u> non existing objects. It is even harder to accept that such practice <i>should be encouraged </i>despite the clearly written rule.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> ....................  I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Now, you are a most talented photographer and have enjoyed great success in this site, including yet another ribbon last night. With that in mind, your attempt at justifying your violation of the rule sounds disingenuous. As to why you would attempt a defense and accuse the SC of being cruel is even more puzzling, do you REALLY think you did not create a wing tip and a strip of background that were not there? The analogy with Enzo''s picture is not even close.<br/> <br/>Please tell me you were joking and may regain respect for you.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by william88: .................... I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot.  You didn''t have to give it up at all! you could have just placed it in your portfolio, or entered it in 1x (for free) or the site you gave a link to Originally posted by william88: .................... As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare.  The rule actually states: "clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections within any capture used.", it is a bit hard to interpret that as allowing for cloning in non existing objects. It is even harder to accept that such practice should be encouraged despite the clearly written rule. Originally posted by william88: ....................  I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.  Now, you are a most talented photographer and have enjoyed great success in this site, including yet another ribbon last night. With that in mind, your attempt at justifying your violation of the rule sounds disingenuous. As to why you would attempt a defense and accuse the SC of being cruel is even more puzzling, do you REALLY think you did not create a wing tip and a strip of background that were not there? The analogy with Enzo''s picture is not even close. Please tell me you were joking and may regain respect for you. ', '2010-11-22 11:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230359, 917505, 59267, '<td valign="top">You guys misunderstood my key point which is "what''s the consequence of too many limits?". It will affect the whole community not just me. I didn''t even send any message to SC to appeal for this shot.<br/> <br/>Please do not distort my words, I didn''t say SC being cruel to this specific shot or not. "Cruel DQs" are totally different words from your "Cruel SCs". You know that. And again I should emphasize my key point is the overall consequence of "cruel rules, cruel DQs and cruel votes", you probably know the consequence already by your own observation over the average number of entries for recent challenges. If you are the owner of a community website, do you think it''s a good trend for you?<br/> <br/>I didn''t compare and say the two DQs were similar or anything (though they were DQed by the same rule), I put that link just for your convenience to read what I have said on 11/09/2010. I just didn''t want to type all those words again. That''s all. If you guys dislike this convenience, I can remove the link. <br/> <br/>You may consider it as a joke when I sang that song. If a boat is sinking and both you and me are on the boat, I will team up with you to repair and save it instead of let it sink.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> .................... I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You didn''t have to give it up at all! you could have just placed it in your portfolio, or entered it in 1x (for free) or the site you gave a link to<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> .................... As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The rule actually states: "clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections within any capture used.", it is a bit hard to interpret that as allowing for <u><i>cloning in</i></u> non existing objects. It is even harder to accept that such practice <i>should be encouraged </i>despite the clearly written rule.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> ....................  I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Now, you are a most talented photographer and have enjoyed great success in this site, including yet another ribbon last night. With that in mind, your attempt at justifying your violation of the rule sounds disingenuous. As to why you would attempt a defense and accuse the SC of being cruel is even more puzzling, do you REALLY think you did not create a wing tip and a strip of background that were not there? The analogy with Enzo''s picture is not even close.<br/> <br/>Please tell me you were joking and may regain respect for you. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'You guys misunderstood my key point which is "what''s the consequence of too many limits?". It will affect the whole community not just me. I didn''t even send any message to SC to appeal for this shot. Please do not distort my words, I didn''t say SC being cruel to this specific shot or not. "Cruel DQs" are totally different words from your "Cruel SCs". You know that. And again I should emphasize my key point is the overall consequence of "cruel rules, cruel DQs and cruel votes", you probably know the consequence already by your own observation over the average number of entries for recent challenges. If you are the owner of a community website, do you think it''s a good trend for you? I didn''t compare and say the two DQs were similar or anything (though they were DQed by the same rule), I put that link just for your convenience to read what I have said on 11/09/2010. I just didn''t want to type all those words again. That''s all. If you guys dislike this convenience, I can remove the link.  You may consider it as a joke when I sang that song. If a boat is sinking and both you and me are on the boat, I will team up with you to repair and save it instead of let it sink. Originally posted by senor_kasper: Originally posted by william88: .................... I was so excited and reluctant to give up this shot.  You didn''t have to give it up at all! you could have just placed it in your portfolio, or entered it in 1x (for free) or the site you gave a link to Originally posted by william88: .................... As I understood from another rule in the advanced editing, using clone stamp to fix minor imperfection is legal and I think that should be encouraged if the shot is rare.  The rule actually states: "clone out incidental power lines, twigs, dust specks, stray hairs, and similar minor imperfections within any capture used.", it is a bit hard to interpret that as allowing for cloning in non existing objects. It is even harder to accept that such practice should be encouraged despite the clearly written rule. Originally posted by william88: ....................  I didn''t create any new feature, I just repair the imperfection.  Now, you are a most talented photographer and have enjoyed great success in this site, including yet another ribbon last night. With that in mind, your attempt at justifying your violation of the rule sounds disingenuous. As to why you would attempt a defense and accuse the SC of being cruel is even more puzzling, do you REALLY think you did not create a wing tip and a strip of background that were not there? The analogy with Enzo''s picture is not even close. Please tell me you were joking and may regain respect for you. ', '2010-11-22 21:16:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230671, 917505, 12253, '<td valign="top">William, sorry about your DQ--it doesn''t reflect poorly on this quality shot.  The DQ is not specifically for cloning the wing tip.  You extended the canvas on the left side and made new "image area".  This is forbidden.  You can never add image area to any of the four sides of the canvas.</td>', 'William, sorry about your DQ--it doesn''t reflect poorly on this quality shot.  The DQ is not specifically for cloning the wing tip.  You extended the canvas on the left side and made new "image area".  This is forbidden.  You can never add image area to any of the four sides of the canvas.', '2010-11-23 02:24:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6245517, 916313, 60495, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 7 but kind of figured it may get under appreciated. When you take the time to look at an image like this one it is hard to not find it fascinating and a very interesting way to capture wildlife.</td>', 'I gave it a 7 but kind of figured it may get under appreciated. When you take the time to look at an image like this one it is hard to not find it fascinating and a very interesting way to capture wildlife.', '2010-12-05 22:56:08.000000', NULL, 0);
