(6663244, 917246, 108580, '<td valign="top">Nice shot using Ext Tubes. It''s not easy. Good background and composition. A bit OE.<br/> <br/>Herman, the DPC "specific rules" of Wildlife V is incorrect. Your shot is perfectly valid despite voters being misled by the "purpose of this competition". You could have photographed a mushroom in the forest and that would have been valid too. It should not then be called a "Wildlife" challenge but rather a "Mammals, birds, reptiles and amphibians" challenge! Unfortunately I learnt this the hard way. Take the challenge literally. Photograph a mammal, bird, reptile or a frog. Voters here are too literal and by voting you down are themselves not following the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_rules.php?RULES_ID=13" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Voting Rules</a>: "...You may not: give an entry a lower score because you believe it violates the Challenge Rules." <br/> <br/><u>Wikipedia (USA)</u>: "Wildlife includes all non-domesticated plants, animals and other organisms." Insects are deemed members of the animal kingdom<br/> <br/><u>Britannica (UK)</u>: "...living things and especially mammals, birds, and fishes that are neither human nor domesticated"<br/> <br/><u>Collins Dictionary (UK)</u>: "wild animals and plants collectively" "You can use wildlife to refer to animals and other living things that live in the wild."<br/> <br/><u>The Free Dictionary (USA)</u>: "Wild animals and vegetation, especially animals living in a natural, undomesticated state."<br/> <br/></td>', 'Nice shot using Ext Tubes. It''s not easy. Good background and composition. A bit OE. Herman, the DPC "specific rules" of Wildlife V is incorrect. Your shot is perfectly valid despite voters being misled by the "purpose of this competition". You could have photographed a mushroom in the forest and that would have been valid too. It should not then be called a "Wildlife" challenge but rather a "Mammals, birds, reptiles and amphibians" challenge! Unfortunately I learnt this the hard way. Take the challenge literally. Photograph a mammal, bird, reptile or a frog. Voters here are too literal and by voting you down are themselves not following the Voting Rules: "...You may not: give an entry a lower score because you believe it violates the Challenge Rules."  Wikipedia (USA): "Wildlife includes all non-domesticated plants, animals and other organisms." Insects are deemed members of the animal kingdom Britannica (UK): "...living things and especially mammals, birds, and fishes that are neither human nor domesticated" Collins Dictionary (UK): "wild animals and plants collectively" "You can use wildlife to refer to animals and other living things that live in the wild." The Free Dictionary (USA): "Wild animals and vegetation, especially animals living in a natural, undomesticated state." ', '2012-02-03 16:08:26.000000', NULL, 0),
